To address this gap, we present a PRISMA-guided systematic review combined with a GIS-centric synthesis. The proposed contributions are: 
- A fully documented PRISMA protocol adapted to spatial data artifacts, with reproducible search strings and inclusion/exclusion rules for GIS and disaster planning literature; 
- A curated dataset of $N_{\mathrm{included}}=62$ studies with metadata on region, platform, stakeholder engagement model, and evaluation metrics; 
- Quantitative meta-synthesis of spatial accuracy, timeliness, and implementation effectiveness, including a composite scoring method; 
- A practical workflow and checklist for municipal authorities and NGOs (illustrated for Jakarta and BNPB collaboration) to operationalize collaborative GIS planning with clear performance targets.
